{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Paul V. Ferkul, National Center for Space Exploration Research\nSandra L. Olson, NASA Glenn Research Center\nMichael C. Johnston, Case Western Reserve University\nJames S. T’ien, Case Western Reserve University\n\nThis work was supported by the NASA Space Life and Physical Sciences Research\nand Applications Division (SLPSRA).\n\nPresented at the 8th US National Combustion Meeting\nPark City, Utah\nMay 19-22, 2013\nFlammability Aspects of Fabric in\nOpposed and Concurrent Air Flow\nin Microgravity", "source_locator": "page:1", "page_number": 1, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-296a077219a92b5f715f1be36000ea6b6ca9ba920749e0473ce20948c9e4c3a7", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 138}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Science Background:\n\n♦ Combustion of solid fuels in micro-\ngravity has been an active area of\nresearch\n\n♦ Numerical models predict that 1-g\nbuoyant flows profoundly affect fuel\nflammability\n\n♦ Ground-based facilities have verified\nthis behavior but only for thin fuels in\nopposed flow\n\n♦ Flow speeds below the buoyant limit\nare of interest", "source_locator": "page:2", "page_number": 2, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-009a1cf922b7a48486d3165b2a74e8b02cf5b2b993630b1203f2718fd92f058b", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 95}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Hypotheses:\n\n♦ Materials in microgravity, with\nadequate ventilation, may burn more\nreadily compared to normal gravity\n\n♦ Testing at constant O2 mole fraction permits studying flame spread and\nextinction at low and high flow speed.", "source_locator": "page:3", "page_number": 3, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-fb4799f0bf918f34f230185d4de4927700168723ec0e06e02aa0a7e8e6ccc3a3", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 62}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Approach:\n\n♦ Microgravity combustion tests were performed\naboard the International Space Station using the\nBASS (Burning and Suppression of Solids)\nhardware.\n\n♦ The wind tunnel was installed in the Microgravity\nScience Glovebox which supplied power, imaging,\nand a level of containment.\n\n♦ Cotton-fiberglass blend fabric samples were\nmounted inside a small wind tunnel which could\nimpose airflow speeds up to 40 cm/s.\n\n♦ The effects of airflow speed on flame appearance,\nflame growth, and spread rates were determined\nin both the opposed and concurrent flow\nconfiguration.", "source_locator": "page:4", "page_number": 4, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-c2110b7cc0ad22a357594cb0e88a202f8a5f8336a65ec2fe29aa8455168ad9a1", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 168}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Science Applications:\n\n Understanding of long-duration microgravity solid material burning and extinction\n Improved strategies for NASA spacecraft materials selection; link actual burn\nbehavior in microgravity to Earth-based selection methods\n Improved combustion computational models used in the design of fire detection\nand suppression systems in microgravity and on Earth\n Validated detailed combustion models in the simpler flow environment of\nmicrogravity build more complex combustion models needed to capture the\nimportant details of flames burning in normal gravity; models have wide\napplicability to the general understanding of many terrestrial combustion\nproblems.", "source_locator": "page:5", "page_number": 5, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-922405b2024b04caa294fbbe1cea9a032ab554d1108a27238030b737a58253ca", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 186}
