{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Comparison of 0-g and 1-g Opposed Flow Flames\n0-g with flow (10 cm/s)\nSteady flame size and spread\nConvex base\nExtended blue zone\n\n1-g\nFlame does not propagate downward", "source_locator": "page:33", "page_number": 33, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-68a4136d327da56de48e5be12cd300b858466e70f22dcae1d7bfbda347e11a47", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 54}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Summary\n\n♦ For the opposed flow configuration, the flame quickly reached steady\nspread for each flow speed, and the spread rate was fastest at an\nintermediate value of flow speed.", "source_locator": "page:34", "page_number": 34, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-16036bedfc26d6feb2015b7139473da67258ebf203225c8cf21c2db5549a04d3", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 50}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Summary\n\n♦ For the opposed flow configuration, the flame quickly reached steady\nspread for each flow speed, and the spread rate was fastest at an\nintermediate value of flow speed.\n\n♦ These tests show the enhanced flammability in microgravity for this\ngeometry, since, in normal gravity air, a flame self-extinguishes in\nthe opposed flow geometry (downward flame spread).", "source_locator": "page:35", "page_number": 35, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-29d201097e88350c3fa81431c200fb1e0243be4d37870783df07a27b3ce2bc5f", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 105}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Summary\n\n♦ For the opposed flow configuration, the flame quickly reached steady\nspread for each flow speed, and the spread rate was fastest at an\nintermediate value of flow speed.\n\n♦ These tests show the enhanced flammability in microgravity for this\ngeometry, since, in normal gravity air, a flame self-extinguishes in\nthe opposed flow geometry (downward flame spread).\n\n♦ For the concurrent flow configuration, a limiting length and steady\nspread rate were obtained only in low flow speeds. For these\nconditions, flame spread rate increased linearly with increasing flow.", "source_locator": "page:36", "page_number": 36, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-a368e647ab586e8b414f5f91f79befe0a0436ab7a11aba1ac0b9e96eb4724d87", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 161}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Summary\n\n♦ For the opposed flow configuration, the flame quickly reached steady\nspread for each flow speed, and the spread rate was fastest at an\nintermediate value of flow speed.\n\n♦ These tests show the enhanced flammability in microgravity for this\ngeometry, since, in normal gravity air, a flame self-extinguishes in\nthe opposed flow geometry (downward flame spread).\n\n♦ For the concurrent flow configuration, a limiting length and steady\nspread rate were obtained only in low flow speeds. For these\nconditions, flame spread rate increased linearly with increasing flow.\n\n♦ This is the first time that detailed transient flame growth data was\nobtained in purely forced flows in microgravity. In addition, by\ndecreasing concurrent flow speed to a very low value (around 1\ncm/s), quenching extinction was observed.", "source_locator": "page:37", "page_number": 37, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-8f1623d20506025c084204f9386de6c1d91ec8315b2a4021bceae27ec0b0004a", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 233}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Summary\n\n♦ For the opposed flow configuration, the flame quickly reached steady\nspread for each flow speed, and the spread rate was fastest at an\nintermediate value of flow speed.\n\n♦ These tests show the enhanced flammability in microgravity for this\ngeometry, since, in normal gravity air, a flame self-extinguishes in\nthe opposed flow geometry (downward flame spread).\n\n♦ For the concurrent flow configuration, a limiting length and steady\nspread rate were obtained only in low flow speeds. For these\nconditions, flame spread rate increased linearly with increasing flow.\n\n♦ This is the first time that detailed transient flame growth data was\nobtained in purely forced flows in microgravity. In addition, by\ndecreasing concurrent flow speed to a very low value (around 1\ncm/s), quenching extinction was observed.\n\n♦ The valuable results from these long-duration experiments validate a\nnumber of theoretical predictions and also provide the data for a\ntransient flame growth model under development.", "source_locator": "page:38", "page_number": 38, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-ca6a855dd1859079ae04e08d841061c345d1c9b1e45880935775542f1c19780a", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 284}
{"source_id": "nasa-d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "content_sha256": "d87675b105c4e44e49b7d375b48bb97dbf3d2b681911f122934a913aa296303d", "experiment": "BASS", "filename": "BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "bass/BASS_Flammability_Aspects_of_Fabric_2013.pdf", "document_type": "publication", "evidence_status": "interpreted", "text": "Fumiaki Takahashi, National Center for Space Exploration Research\nBob Hawersaat, NASA Glenn Research Center\nJay Owens, National Center for Space Exploration Research\nTibor Lorik, ZIN Technologies\nChuck Bunnell, ZIN Technologies\nDennis Siedlak, Georgia Institute of Technology\nCarol Reynolds, NASA Marshall Space Flight Center\nDon Pettit, NASA Johnson Space Center\nJoe Acaba, NASA Johnson Space Center\nSuni Williams,NASA Johnson Space Center\n\nAcknowledgments:", "source_locator": "page:39", "page_number": 39, "document_metadata": {"title": "BASS POIWG Presentation", "author": "Paul Ferkul", "created": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "modified": "D:20131101114402-04'00'", "producer": "Microsoft® PowerPoint® 2010"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26", "source_accession": "PSI-26", "chunk_id": "chunk-907d7384180a0c57805b8393f2f23fcc5c49c5b4530884cdcf649541b868ff39", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 130}
